IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bgg3-nouns`
IMPORT `bgg4-nouns`
IMPORT `bgg4-time-limit`

-- bgg4-cantonal: BGG 4. Kapitel, 7. Abschnitt, Kantonales Verfahren (Art. 110 to 112).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively; nobody's point of view.
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN (or MAYBE DATE): JUST TRUE (the text says yes), JUST FALSE (the text says no,
-- tagged FALSE-kind), NOTHING (not covered, tagged NOTHING-kind).  See bgg4-appealable for the key.
--
-- Arts 110 and 111 put duties on the cantons ("gewährleisten sie", "muss ... können").  The text states no
-- consequence for the person if a canton did not comply, so a duty not done is NOTHING, never JUST FALSE
-- (fork F27, the reading of chapter 3's F5: a bare must not done).  The cantons' actor is chapter 3's `Canton`, used and not copied.
-- Art 112 is about the written decision the person receives; a decision that falls short of paragraph 1 is
-- one that "den Anforderungen von Absatz 1 nicht genügt" (paragraph 3), which is the text's own "no".

§ `Art 110 Beurteilung durch richterliche Behörde (review by a judicial authority)`

-- src:134 | Soweit die Kantone nach diesem Gesetz als letzte kantonale Instanz ein Gericht einzusetzen haben, gewährleisten sie, dass dieses selbst oder eine vorgängig zuständige andere richterliche Behörde den Sachverhalt frei prüft und das massgebende Recht von Amtes wegen anwendet.
@ref Art. 110 BGG (src:134)
GIVEN `the canton must set up a court as last cantonal instance under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN                                  -- Soweit die Kantone nach diesem Gesetz als letzte kantonale Instanz ein Gericht einzusetzen haben
      `the court or a previously competent judicial authority freely reviews the facts` IS A BOOLEAN                         -- den Sachverhalt frei prüft
      `the court or a previously competent judicial authority applies the governing law of its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN      -- das massgebende Recht von Amtes wegen anwendet
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 110 the canton has ensured the review by a judicial authority` MEANS
    IF `the canton must set up a court as last cantonal instance under this Act` AND `the court or a previously competent judicial authority freely reviews the facts` AND `the court or a previously competent judicial authority applies the governing law of its own motion`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a duty on the cantons ("gewährleisten sie"), limited by "Soweit"; the text states no consequence for the person if a canton did not comply (a bare must not done: fork F27, the reading of chapter 3's F5)

-- The cantons' duty in Art 110, as a regulative rule.  No time limit is stated and none is invented.
-- src:134 | Soweit die Kantone nach diesem Gesetz als letzte kantonale Instanz ein Gericht einzusetzen haben, gewährleisten sie, dass dieses selbst oder eine vorgängig zuständige andere richterliche Behörde den Sachverhalt frei prüft und das massgebende Recht von Amtes wegen anwendet.
@ref Art. 110 BGG (the duty) (src:134)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor in chapter 3` `Cantonal act in chapter 4`
`Art 110 the cantons' duty to ensure the review by a judicial authority` MEANS
    PARTY Canton
    MUST `ensure that the court or a previously competent judicial authority freely reviews the facts and applies the law of its own motion`

§ `Art 111 Einheit des Verfahrens (unity of the proceedings)`

-- src:137 | 1 Wer zur Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht berechtigt ist, muss sich am Verfahren vor allen kantonalen Vorinstanzen als Partei beteiligen können.
@ref Art. 111(1) BGG (src:137)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN         -- Wer zur Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht berechtigt ist: answered by chapter 3 (see bgg4-seams)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 111(1) the person entitled to appeal must be able to take part as a party before all cantonal lower instances` MEANS
    IF `the person is entitled to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph reaches only "Wer zur Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht berechtigt ist"; for anyone else it says nothing

-- src:137 | 1 Wer zur Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht berechtigt ist, muss sich am Verfahren vor allen kantonalen Vorinstanzen als Partei beteiligen können.
@ref Art. 111(1) BGG (the canton has complied) (src:137)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person could take part as a party before all cantonal lower instances` IS A BOOLEAN        -- sich am Verfahren vor allen kantonalen Vorinstanzen als Partei beteiligen können
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 111(1) the canton has let the person take part as a party before all cantonal lower instances` MEANS
    IF `the person is entitled to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` AND `the person could take part as a party before all cantonal lower instances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a duty on the cantons ("muss ... können"); the text states no consequence for the person if a canton did not comply (a bare must not done: fork F27, the reading of chapter 3's F5)

-- src:137 | 1 Wer zur Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht berechtigt ist, muss sich am Verfahren vor allen kantonalen Vorinstanzen als Partei beteiligen können.
@ref Art. 111(1) BGG (the duty) (src:137)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor in chapter 3` `Cantonal act in chapter 4`
`Art 111(1) the cantons' duty to let a person entitled to appeal take part as a party` MEANS
    PARTY Canton
    MUST `let a person entitled to appeal take part as a party before all cantonal lower instances`

-- src:138 | 2 Bundesbehörden, die zur Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht berechtigt sind, können die Rechtsmittel des kantonalen Rechts ergreifen und sich vor jeder kantonalen Instanz am Verfahren beteiligen, wenn sie dies beantragen.
@ref Art. 111(2) BGG (src:138)
GIVEN `the authority is a federal authority entitled to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN       -- Bundesbehörden, die zur Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht berechtigt sind
      `the federal authority applied to take part` IS A BOOLEAN                                                  -- wenn sie dies beantragen
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 111(2) the federal authority may take the remedies of cantonal law and take part before every cantonal instance` MEANS
    IF `the authority is a federal authority entitled to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` AND `the federal authority applied to take part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power ("können") for federal authorities entitled to appeal, "wenn sie dies beantragen"; a power whose stated gate failed answers NOTHING, not a "may not" (ruling of 2026-11-12, limb 1; fork F17)

-- src:139 | 3 Die unmittelbare Vorinstanz des Bundesgerichts muss mindestens die Rügen nach den Artikeln 95–98 prüfen können. …[^15]
@ref Art. 111(3) BGG (first sentence) (src:139)
GIVEN `the immediate lower instance of the Federal Supreme Court can examine the complaints under Art 95 to 98` IS A BOOLEAN       -- mindestens die Rügen nach den Artikeln 95–98 prüfen können
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 111(3) the immediate lower instance can examine at least the complaints under Art 95 to 98` MEANS
    IF `the immediate lower instance of the Federal Supreme Court can examine the complaints under Art 95 to 98`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a duty ("muss ... prüfen können"); the text states no consequence for the person if the lower instance cannot (a bare must not done: fork F27, the reading of chapter 3's F5)

-- The second sentence of paragraph 3 is shown repealed ("…" and footnote 15).  A labelled stub, no operative outcome: nothing calls it.
-- src:139 | 3 Die unmittelbare Vorinstanz des Bundesgerichts muss mindestens die Rügen nach den Artikeln 95–98 prüfen können. …[^15]
-- src:165 | [^15] Zweiter Satz aufgehoben durch Anhang 1 Ziff. II 2 der Zivilprozessordnung vom 19. Dez. 2008, mit Wirkung seit 1. Jan. 2011 (AS 2010 1739; BBl 2006 7221).
@ref Art. 111(3) BGG (second sentence, repealed) (src:139) (src:165)
`Art 111(3) second sentence is shown repealed in this text and is not encoded` MEANS
        "…"
    ... "Zweiter Satz aufgehoben durch Anhang 1 Ziff. II 2 der Zivilprozessordnung vom 19. Dez. 2008, mit Wirkung seit 1. Jan. 2011"

-- src:139 | 3 Die unmittelbare Vorinstanz des Bundesgerichts muss mindestens die Rügen nach den Artikeln 95–98 prüfen können. …[^15]
@ref Art. 111(3) BGG (the duty) (src:139)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor in chapter 3` `Cantonal act in chapter 4`
`Art 111(3) the cantons' duty to let the immediate lower instance examine the complaints under Art 95 to 98` MEANS
    PARTY Canton
    MUST `let the immediate lower instance examine at least the complaints under Art 95 to 98`

§ `Art 112 Eröffnung der Entscheide (notification of decisions)`

-- Paragraph (1): the written decision and what it contains.  A decision that is not subject to appeal is not reached
-- ("Entscheide, die der Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht unterliegen"): NOTHING.  A requirement met is JUST TRUE; a requirement not met
-- is JUST FALSE, because paragraph 3 calls such a decision one "der den Anforderungen von Absatz 1 nicht genügt" (fork F23).
-- src:142 | 1 Entscheide, die der Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht unterliegen, sind den Parteien schriftlich zu eröffnen. Sie müssen enthalten:
@ref Art. 112(1) BGG (written notification) (src:142)
GIVEN `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision was notified to the parties in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(1) the decision is notified to the parties in writing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph reaches only "Entscheide, die der Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht unterliegen"
        IF `the decision was notified to the parties in writing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "sind den Parteien schriftlich zu eröffnen"; paragraph 3 calls a decision that falls short a decision that "den Anforderungen von Absatz 1 nicht genügt"

-- src:142 | 1 Entscheide, die der Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht unterliegen, sind den Parteien schriftlich zu eröffnen. Sie müssen enthalten:
-- src:143 | a. die Begehren, die Begründung, die Beweisvorbringen und Prozesserklärungen der Parteien, soweit sie nicht aus den Akten hervorgehen;
@ref Art. 112(1)(a) BGG (src:142-143)
GIVEN `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision contains the claims, the reasoning, the evidence offered and the procedural declarations of the parties` IS A BOOLEAN       -- die Begehren, die Begründung, die Beweisvorbringen und Prozesserklärungen der Parteien
      `those matters appear from the files` IS A BOOLEAN                                                                                         -- soweit sie nicht aus den Akten hervorgehen
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(1)(a) the decision contains the claims, reasoning, evidence and procedural declarations of the parties` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph reaches only decisions subject to appeal
        IF `the decision contains the claims, the reasoning, the evidence offered and the procedural declarations of the parties` OR `those matters appear from the files` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Sie müssen enthalten: a. ..., soweit sie nicht aus den Akten hervorgehen"; paragraph 3: "den Anforderungen von Absatz 1 nicht genügt"

-- src:142 | 1 Entscheide, die der Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht unterliegen, sind den Parteien schriftlich zu eröffnen. Sie müssen enthalten:
-- src:144 | b. die massgebenden Gründe tatsächlicher und rechtlicher Art, insbesondere die Angabe der angewendeten Gesetzesbestimmungen;
@ref Art. 112(1)(b) BGG (src:142) (src:144)
GIVEN `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision contains the governing reasons of fact and of law, in particular the statutory provisions applied` IS A BOOLEAN       -- die massgebenden Gründe tatsächlicher und rechtlicher Art, insbesondere die Angabe der angewendeten Gesetzesbestimmungen
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(1)(b) the decision contains the governing reasons of fact and law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph reaches only decisions subject to appeal
        IF `the decision contains the governing reasons of fact and of law, in particular the statutory provisions applied` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Sie müssen enthalten: ... b. die massgebenden Gründe tatsächlicher und rechtlicher Art"; paragraph 3: "den Anforderungen von Absatz 1 nicht genügt"

-- src:142 | 1 Entscheide, die der Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht unterliegen, sind den Parteien schriftlich zu eröffnen. Sie müssen enthalten:
-- src:145 | c. das Dispositiv;
@ref Art. 112(1)(c) BGG (src:142) (src:145)
GIVEN `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision contains the operative part` IS A BOOLEAN                       -- das Dispositiv
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(1)(c) the decision contains the operative part` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph reaches only decisions subject to appeal
        IF `the decision contains the operative part` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Sie müssen enthalten: ... c. das Dispositiv"; paragraph 3: "den Anforderungen von Absatz 1 nicht genügt"

-- src:142 | 1 Entscheide, die der Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht unterliegen, sind den Parteien schriftlich zu eröffnen. Sie müssen enthalten:
-- src:146 | d. eine Rechtsmittelbelehrung einschliesslich Angabe des Streitwerts, soweit dieses Gesetz eine Streitwertgrenze vorsieht.
@ref Art. 112(1)(d) BGG (src:142) (src:146)
GIVEN `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision contains a notice of the available legal remedies` IS A BOOLEAN         -- eine Rechtsmittelbelehrung
      `this Act provides a value limit for the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN                         -- soweit dieses Gesetz eine Streitwertgrenze vorsieht: answered by chapter 3 (see bgg4-seams)
      `the notice states the value in dispute` IS A BOOLEAN                                 -- einschliesslich Angabe des Streitwerts
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(1)(d) the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where this Act provides a value limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph reaches only decisions subject to appeal
        IF `the decision contains a notice of the available legal remedies` AND ((NOT `this Act provides a value limit for the appeal`) OR `the notice states the value in dispute`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Sie müssen enthalten: ... d. eine Rechtsmittelbelehrung einschliesslich Angabe des Streitwerts, soweit dieses Gesetz eine Streitwertgrenze vorsieht"; paragraph 3: "den Anforderungen von Absatz 1 nicht genügt"

-- src:142 | 1 Entscheide, die der Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht unterliegen, sind den Parteien schriftlich zu eröffnen. Sie müssen enthalten:
-- src:143 | a. die Begehren, die Begründung, die Beweisvorbringen und Prozesserklärungen der Parteien, soweit sie nicht aus den Akten hervorgehen;
-- src:144 | b. die massgebenden Gründe tatsächlicher und rechtlicher Art, insbesondere die Angabe der angewendeten Gesetzesbestimmungen;
-- src:145 | c. das Dispositiv;
-- src:146 | d. eine Rechtsmittelbelehrung einschliesslich Angabe des Streitwerts, soweit dieses Gesetz eine Streitwertgrenze vorsieht.
@ref Art. 112(1) BGG (src:142-146)
GIVEN `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision was notified to the parties in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision contains the claims, the reasoning, the evidence offered and the procedural declarations of the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those matters appear from the files` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision contains the governing reasons of fact and of law, in particular the statutory provisions applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision contains the operative part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision contains a notice of the available legal remedies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Act provides a value limit for the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the value in dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(1) the decision meets the requirements of paragraph 1` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph reaches only decisions subject to appeal
        IF     `Art 112(1) the decision is notified to the parties in writing` `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` `the decision was notified to the parties in writing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `Art 112(1)(a) the decision contains the claims, reasoning, evidence and procedural declarations of the parties` `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` `the decision contains the claims, the reasoning, the evidence offered and the procedural declarations of the parties` `those matters appear from the files` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `Art 112(1)(b) the decision contains the governing reasons of fact and law` `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` `the decision contains the governing reasons of fact and of law, in particular the statutory provisions applied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `Art 112(1)(c) the decision contains the operative part` `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` `the decision contains the operative part` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `Art 112(1)(d) the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where this Act provides a value limit` `the decision is subject to appeal to the Federal Supreme Court` `the decision contains a notice of the available legal remedies` `this Act provides a value limit for the appeal` `the notice states the value in dispute` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a decision short of any requirement of paragraph 1 is one "der den Anforderungen von Absatz 1 nicht genügt" (paragraph 3)

-- The authority's duty to notify in writing, as a regulative rule.  No time limit is stated and none is invented.
-- src:142 | 1 Entscheide, die der Beschwerde an das Bundesgericht unterliegen, sind den Parteien schriftlich zu eröffnen. Sie müssen enthalten:
@ref Art. 112(1) BGG (the duty) (src:142)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor in chapter 4` `Act in chapter 4`
`Art 112(1) the cantonal authority's duty to notify the decision to the parties in writing` MEANS
    PARTY `Lower instance`
    MUST `notify the decision to the parties in writing`

-- Paragraph (2), first sentence: notification without reasons.
-- src:147 | 2 Sofern es das Bundesrecht oder das kantonale Recht vorsieht, eröffnet die Behörde ihren Entscheid in der Regel zeitnah und ohne Begründung.[^16] Die Parteien können in diesem Fall innert 30 Tagen eine vollständige Ausfertigung verlangen. Der Entscheid ist nicht vollstreckbar, solange nicht entweder diese Frist unbenützt abgelaufen oder die vollständige Ausfertigung eröffnet worden ist.
@ref Art. 112(2) BGG (first sentence) (src:147)
GIVEN `federal law or cantonal law provides for notification without reasons` IS A BOOLEAN       -- Sofern es das Bundesrecht oder das kantonale Recht vorsieht: both are outside the sources
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(2) the authority may notify the decision promptly and without reasons` MEANS
    IF `federal law or cantonal law provides for notification without reasons`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Sofern es das Bundesrecht oder das kantonale Recht vorsieht" points at federal and cantonal law, which are outside the sources; where neither provides for it the sentence is silent, and a gate that failed answers NOTHING, not a "may not" (ruling of 2026-11-12, limb 1; fork F24); "in der Regel" leaves exceptions open

-- Paragraph (2), second sentence: the 30 days in which a party can demand the complete version.  Counted as in bgg4-time-limit
-- (the day after the notification is day 1; fork F9) and moved by the days that rules outside this chapter leave out of the count (fork F10).
-- src:147 | 2 Sofern es das Bundesrecht oder das kantonale Recht vorsieht, eröffnet die Behörde ihren Entscheid in der Regel zeitnah und ohne Begründung.[^16] Die Parteien können in diesem Fall innert 30 Tagen eine vollständige Ausfertigung verlangen. Der Entscheid ist nicht vollstreckbar, solange nicht entweder diese Frist unbenützt abgelaufen oder die vollständige Ausfertigung eröffnet worden ist.
@ref Art. 112(2) BGG (second sentence) (src:147)
GIVEN `the decision was notified without reasons under the first sentence` IS A BOOLEAN         -- in diesem Fall
      `the day the decision without reasons was notified` IS A DATE
      `the days that rules outside this chapter leave out of the count` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 112(2) the last day to demand the complete version` MEANS
    IF `the decision was notified without reasons under the first sentence`
    THEN JUST (`Art 100(1) the last day of a period counted from the start day` `the day the decision without reasons was notified` 30 `the days that rules outside this chapter leave out of the count`)
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the 30 days run "in diesem Fall", the case of a decision notified without reasons

-- src:147 | 2 Sofern es das Bundesrecht oder das kantonale Recht vorsieht, eröffnet die Behörde ihren Entscheid in der Regel zeitnah und ohne Begründung.[^16] Die Parteien können in diesem Fall innert 30 Tagen eine vollständige Ausfertigung verlangen. Der Entscheid ist nicht vollstreckbar, solange nicht entweder diese Frist unbenützt abgelaufen oder die vollständige Ausfertigung eröffnet worden ist.
@ref Art. 112(2) BGG (the demand is in time) (src:147)
GIVEN `the decision was notified without reasons under the first sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the decision without reasons was notified` IS A DATE
      `the days that rules outside this chapter leave out of the count` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the party demanded the complete version` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(2) the demand for the complete version is in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the decision was notified without reasons under the first sentence` THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in diesem Fall"
        IF `the day the party demanded the complete version` LESS THAN `the day the decision without reasons was notified` THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text speaks of a demand "innert 30 Tagen" after the notification and says nothing of a demand before it
        IF `the day the party demanded the complete version` AT MOST (`Art 100(1) the last day of a period counted from the start day` `the day the decision without reasons was notified` 30 `the days that rules outside this chapter leave out of the count`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a period the text fixes in its own words ("innert 30 Tagen"); outside it the answer is JUST FALSE (periods ruling (a) of 2026-11-05)

-- The party's permission, as a regulative rule: "Die Parteien können in diesem Fall innert 30 Tagen eine vollständige Ausfertigung verlangen".
-- src:147 | 2 Sofern es das Bundesrecht oder das kantonale Recht vorsieht, eröffnet die Behörde ihren Entscheid in der Regel zeitnah und ohne Begründung.[^16] Die Parteien können in diesem Fall innert 30 Tagen eine vollständige Ausfertigung verlangen. Der Entscheid ist nicht vollstreckbar, solange nicht entweder diese Frist unbenützt abgelaufen oder die vollständige Ausfertigung eröffnet worden ist.
@ref Art. 112(2) BGG (the permission) (src:147)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor in chapter 4` `Act in chapter 4`
`Art 112(2) the parties' permission to demand the complete version within 30 days` MEANS
    PARTY `Party to the proceedings`
    MAY `demand the complete version of the decision`
    WITHIN 30

-- Paragraph (2), third sentence: the bar on enforcement.  "nicht vollstreckbar, solange nicht entweder ... oder ..." bars enforcement
-- until one of two things has happened.  The function answers whether the BAR STILL APPLIES: JUST TRUE while it does, JUST FALSE once it is
-- lifted.  JUST FALSE does not say the decision may be enforced: the text bars enforcement until then and says nothing of what other law
-- requires after it (fork F25).
-- src:147 | 2 Sofern es das Bundesrecht oder das kantonale Recht vorsieht, eröffnet die Behörde ihren Entscheid in der Regel zeitnah und ohne Begründung.[^16] Die Parteien können in diesem Fall innert 30 Tagen eine vollständige Ausfertigung verlangen. Der Entscheid ist nicht vollstreckbar, solange nicht entweder diese Frist unbenützt abgelaufen oder die vollständige Ausfertigung eröffnet worden ist.
@ref Art. 112(2) BGG (third sentence) (src:147)
GIVEN `the decision was notified without reasons under the first sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the decision without reasons was notified` IS A DATE
      `the days that rules outside this chapter leave out of the count` IS A NUMBER
      `a party demanded the complete version within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complete version of the decision has been notified` IS A BOOLEAN             -- die vollständige Ausfertigung eröffnet worden ist
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(2) the bar on enforcing the decision still applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the decision was notified without reasons under the first sentence` THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence follows "in diesem Fall", the decision notified without reasons
        IF `the complete version of the decision has been notified` THEN JUST FALSE                 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "solange nicht ... die vollständige Ausfertigung eröffnet worden ist": the bar is lifted
        IF (NOT `a party demanded the complete version within the period`) AND `the day asked about` GREATER THAN (`Art 100(1) the last day of a period counted from the start day` `the day the decision without reasons was notified` 30 `the days that rules outside this chapter leave out of the count`) THEN JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "solange nicht ... diese Frist unbenützt abgelaufen ... ist": the bar is lifted
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE       -- "Der Entscheid ist nicht vollstreckbar"

-- Paragraph (3): the Federal Supreme Court's power.
-- src:148 | 3 Das Bundesgericht kann einen Entscheid, der den Anforderungen von Absatz 1 nicht genügt, an die kantonale Behörde zur Verbesserung zurückweisen oder aufheben.
@ref Art. 112(3) BGG (src:148)
GIVEN `the decision does not meet the requirements of paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN        -- der den Anforderungen von Absatz 1 nicht genügt
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(3) the Court may remit the decision for improvement or quash it` MEANS
    IF `the decision does not meet the requirements of paragraph 1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power ("kann ... zurückweisen oder aufheben") whose stated gate failed answers NOTHING, not a "may not" (ruling of 2026-11-12, limb 1; fork F17)

-- Paragraph (4): the Federal Council decides which decisions go to the federal authorities.  The Federal Council's determination is
-- outside the sources, so it is an input (an answer the person or the caller supplies).
-- src:149 | 4 Für die Gebiete, in denen Bundesbehörden zur Beschwerde berechtigt sind, bestimmt der Bundesrat, welche Entscheide ihnen die kantonalen Behörden zu eröffnen haben.
@ref Art. 112(4) BGG (src:149)
GIVEN `the field is one in which federal authorities are entitled to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN        -- Für die Gebiete, in denen Bundesbehörden zur Beschwerde berechtigt sind
      `the Federal Council has determined that decisions of this kind are notified to the federal authority` IS A BOOLEAN   -- bestimmt der Bundesrat, welche Entscheide ihnen die kantonalen Behörden zu eröffnen haben
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 112(4) the cantonal authority must notify the decision to the federal authority` MEANS
    IF `the field is one in which federal authorities are entitled to appeal` AND `the Federal Council has determined that decisions of this kind are notified to the federal authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): which decisions the cantonal authorities must notify is for the Federal Council to determine (the determination is outside the sources); where it has not, the paragraph says nothing
